### Spring REST Endpoint

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/retrieve")
class RetrievalController {
    private final Retriever sparseRetriever;
    private final Retriever denseRetriever;
    private final FusionStrategy fusionStrategy;
    private final ReRanker reRanker;

    @GetMapping
    public ResponseEntity<List<Document>> get(@RequestParam String q,
                                              @RequestParam(defaultValue="10") int topN) {
        List<DocumentScore> sparse = sparseRetriever.retrieve(q, topN);
        List<DocumentScore> dense  = denseRetriever.retrieve(q, topN);
        List<DocumentScore> fused  = fusionStrategy.fuse(sparse, dense);
        List<Document> finalDocs = reRanker.reRank(q, fused, topN);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(finalDocs);
    }
}
```

### Architecture Pattern (Resilience4j + Axon + Kafka)

```java
@Component
class RetrievalOrchestrator {
    @Autowired
    private CircuitBreakerFactory cbFactory;
    @Autowired
    private EventBus eventBus; // Axon EventBus
    @Autowired
    private KafkaTemplate<String, FusionEvent> kafkaTemplate;

    @Retryable(maxAttempts=3)
    public List<DocumentScore> orchestrate(String query, int topN) {
        CircuitBreaker cb = cbFactory.create("retrieval");
        List<DocumentScore> sparse = cb.executeSupplier(() -> sparseRetriever.retrieve(query, topN));
        List<DocumentScore> dense  = cb.executeSupplier(() -> denseRetriever.retrieve(query, topN));
        List<DocumentScore> fused  = fusionStrategy.fuse(sparse, dense);
        eventBus.publish(new FusionEvent(query, fused));
        kafkaTemplate.send("fusion-events", new FusionEvent(query, fused));
        return fused;
    }
}
```

### DSA – Three Java Problem Solutions

```java
// 1. Merge two sorted lists of DocumentScore by score
List<DocumentScore> mergeSorted(List<DocumentScore> a, List<DocumentScore> b) {
    List<DocumentScore> merged = new ArrayList<>();
    int i=0,j=0;
    while(i<a.size() && j<b.size()){
        if(a.get(i).score >= b.get(j).score) merged.add(a.get(i++));
        else merged.add(b.get(j++));
    }
    while(i<a.size()) merged.add(a.get(i++));
    while(j<b.size()) merged.add(b.get(j++));
    return merged;
}

// 2. Weighted sum of two score lists
List<DocumentScore> weightedSum(List<DocumentScore> sparse, List<DocumentScore> dense,
                                 double alpha, double beta) {
    Map<String, Double> map = new HashMap<>();
    for(DocumentScore ds : sparse) map.merge(ds.docId, alpha*ds.score, Double::sum);
    for(DocumentScore ds : dense)  map.merge(ds.docId, beta*ds.score, Double::sum);
    return map.entrySet().stream()
              .map(e -> new DocumentScore(e.getKey(), e.getValue(), Source.MIXED))
              .sorted(Comparator.comparingDouble(d -> -d.score))
              .collect(Collectors.toList());
}

// 3. Top‑k priority queue for re‑ranking
List<DocumentScore> topK(List<DocumentScore> candidates, int k) {
    PriorityQueue<DocumentScore> pq = new PriorityQueue<>(Comparator.comparingDouble(d -> d.score));
    for(DocumentScore d : candidates){
        if(pq.size()<k) pq.offer(d);
        else if(d.score > pq.peek().score){ pq.poll(); pq.offer(d); }
    }
    List<DocumentScore> result = new ArrayList<>(pq);
    result.sort(Comparator.comparingDouble(d -> -d.score));
    return result;
}
```

### Python ML Snippet (Vector Similarity)

```python
import numpy as np

def cosine_similarity(q_vec, d_vec):
    q_norm = np.linalg.norm(q_vec)
    d_norm = np.linalg.norm(d_vec)
    return np.dot(q_vec, d_vec) / (q_norm * d_norm)
```

